▶️ How to Run the Project

Step 1: Clone the repository.

git clone https://github.com/pushkarajumbare/Food-Delivery-Time-Prediction-using-logistic-regression.git

Step 2: Open the project folder.

cd Food-Delivery-Time-Prediction-using-logistic-regression

Step 3: Install the required libraries.

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib scikit-learn jupyter

Step 4: Download the dataset from Kaggle and place "Food_Delivery_Times.csv" in the project directory.

Step 5: Open the Jupyter Notebook.

jupyter notebook Untitled2.ipynb

Step 6: Run all notebook cells to train and evaluate the Logistic Regression model.

📝 Conclusion

The Logistic Regression model successfully classified food delivery times into quicker and slower categories based on the dataset median of 55.5 minutes.

With 92% accuracy and a ROC-AUC score of 0.9692, the model demonstrated strong classification performance. Features such as distance, weather, traffic conditions, preparation time, and courier experience help identify whether a delivery is likely to be quicker or slower.

This project demonstrates how machine learning can be applied to food delivery data to support delivery-time analysis and better operational planning.

